claimed: chunk-bench-matrix — the chunked/flushing stream work measured properly and in company: (a) an edge-case suite for chunking and Flush (empty, one element, exactly a chunk, chunk +/- 1, one side empty, a failing source, an early-stopping consumer, a boundary at the very start/end, two in a row); (b) a benchmark across the real axes -- chunked on/off x flush on/off x a fast and a SLOW source, the last being where a timeout flush is the whole point; (c) the same benchmarks written on fs2 (chunkN, groupWithin) and ZIO (grouped, groupedWithin), which have direct equivalents, so the comparison is like-for-like rather than our feature against their absence; (d) docs/benchmarks.md section and table, and the guide pointer.
